HOW MANGO COUNTS
  Energy = fast moves × the fast move's energy, minus charged moves thrown (max 100).
  Turns are 0.5s. The opponent is assumed to throw PvPoke's recommended fast move nonstop.
  - The clock stops when your charged move buttons vanish (either side's charged move, a
    faint) and restarts when they're back. Stops/restarts are back-dated (settings below)
    because the screen is read 4 times a second and changed up to 0.25s earlier.
  - Your charged move waits for your fast move to finish; the battle runs on until then.
  - When you throw, they get their finished fast moves plus the one in progress, including
    when your moves line up (they start one on the turn your charged move takes).
    Not when they throw on the same turn (their charged move in the same stop as yours).
  - When they throw, only finished fast moves count; then they start fresh.
  - A switch takes 1 turn. 0 for a fainted Pokémon's replacement, or when their charged
    move came last in the stop and the switch shows as the battle restarts. After your
    Pokémon faints, their switch (theirs still in) costs a turn.
  - Benched Pokémon keep their energy.

SETTINGS (fitted on the hand counts of all recorded battles)
  The battle starts 0.200s after "GO" is first read.
  Battle stops 0.125s before your buttons are first read as gone.
  Your charged move freezes the battle 0.750s before "Get Ready!" is read.
  Battle resumes 0.250s before your buttons are read again (0.250s after a faint).

